From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tarun Lalwani <tarunlalwani@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: fix: guard DevTools Fetch resume and body collection

Temporary patch. Drop it when Electron rolls a Chromium that contains
https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8084482.

Fetch interception at the Response stage had two crashes:

1. A failed request with a body could be continued, and the
   InterceptionJob destroyed, re-entrantly during the synchronous
   RequestBodyCollector::Collect() in NotifyClient(). The completions are
   now bound with a WeakPtr and NotifyClient() returns if the job is gone.

2. Fetch.getResponseBody followed by continueResponse could resume
   client_receiver_ after upstream OnComplete() had reset it, a null
   dereference in MultiplexRouter.

The fix tracks upstream completion explicitly in completion_status_
instead of inferring it from client_receiver_.is_bound(). The client is
resumed only while completion has not arrived, and a buffered response is
sent once body EOF, upstream completion and DevTools continuation have all
happened, in any order. The new invariant CHECKs are NotFatalUntil::M162.

